WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:03.200
SmartVest Investing Academy.

2
00:00:03.150 --> 00:00:06.375
Lesson 1: What is Investment?

3
00:00:06.375 --> 00:00:15.537
Have you ever wondered why simply saving money in a bank account or cash locker is no longer enough to secure your financial future?

4
00:00:15.537 --> 00:00:20.587
Saving means keeping your unspent income safe in low-risk places.

5
00:00:20.587 --> 00:00:27.025
While saving preserves your nominal rupees, it suffers from a hidden threat called inflation.

6
00:00:27.025 --> 00:00:37.900
Over time, inflation causes prices of everyday goods, housing, and healthcare to rise, which constantly reduces the purchasing power of your idle cash.

7
00:00:37.900 --> 00:00:56.462
Investing, on the other hand, means deploying your money into productive assets—such as company stocks, government and corporate bonds, mutual funds, or real estate—with the expectation that they will generate income, pay dividends, or appreciate in value over time.

8
00:00:56.462 --> 00:00:59.625
Let us look at a practical example.

9
00:00:59.625 --> 00:01:02.800
Imagine you have ₹10,000 today.

10
00:01:02.800 --> 00:01:11.138
If you keep this ₹10,000 in a zero-interest locker for 10 years, you will still have exactly ₹10,000.

11
00:01:11.138 --> 00:01:21.088
However, if inflation averages 6% per year, things that cost ₹10,000 today will cost nearly ₹18,000 in a decade.

12
00:01:21.088 --> 00:01:25.850
Your saved cash lost nearly half its real purchasing power.

13
00:01:25.850 --> 00:01:40.875
If, instead, you invest that ₹10,000 into productive businesses or diversified mutual funds earning potential economic returns, your capital works alongside economic expansion to outpace inflation.

14
00:01:40.875 --> 00:01:47.912
A common beginner misunderstanding is thinking that investing is just gambling or speculative trading.

15
00:01:47.912 --> 00:01:50.012
That is incorrect.

16
00:01:50.013 --> 00:01:56.050
Speculation is betting on short-term price swings without regard to intrinsic value.

17
00:01:56.050 --> 00:02:05.900
Genuine investing is providing capital to real, productive businesses that create goods, employ people, and generate long-term profits.

18
00:02:05.900 --> 00:02:10.013
Remember: investing is not guaranteed profit.

19
00:02:10.012 --> 00:02:16.688
Asset prices fluctuate, and market downturns are a natural part of economic cycles.

20
00:02:16.688 --> 00:02:25.200
The goal of investing is to thoughtfully balance risk and time horizon so that your wealth grows sustainably over the long run.

21
00:02:25.200 --> 00:02:34.612
Saving preserves cash for today's emergencies; investing puts your capital to work to protect and grow your purchasing power for tomorrow.

22
00:02:34.613 --> 00:02:37.663
SmartVest Investing Academy.

23
00:02:37.662 --> 00:02:39.487
Learn first.

24
00:02:39.488 --> 00:02:41.938
Invest with understanding.
